pective.', 'languages_used': ['en'], 'perspectives': [{'language': 'en', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kosmos_1223', 'key_points': ['**Cold‑War early‑warning asset:**\\u202fKosmos\\u202f1223 was a Soviet US‑K‑type “Oko” missile‑launch detection satellite, equipped with optical telescopes and infrared sensors to spot incoming missiles.', '**Launch & orbit:**\\u202fLifted on 27\\u202fNov\\u202f1980 by a Molniya‑M/2BL rocket from Plesetsk, it was placed into a highly elliptical Molniya orbit (≈\\u202f663\\u202fkm ×\\u202f39\\u202f700\\u202fkm, 62.9° inclination, 12‑hour period).', '**Short‑lived service:**\\u202fAlthough originally slated for a four‑year mission, the spacecraft was deactivated on 11\\u202fAug\\u202f1982—less than two years after launch.', '**Identification:**\\u202fAfter launch it received the designation Kosmos\\u202f1223, the international designator 1980‑095A, and US\\u202fSpace Command catalog number 12078.', '**Contextual note:**\\u202fKosmos\\u202f1223 is one of many satellites in the extensive Oko early‑warning program that populated the “Kosmos” series of Soviet spacecraft.']}]}}, {'seed': {'name': 'Kosmos 1581', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kosmos_1581'}, 'extracted': {'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kosmos_1581', 'name': 'Kosmos 1581', 'years': '1984', 'short_description': 'Kosmos 1581 was a Soviet US‑K missile early‑warning satellite launched on 3\\u202fJuly\\u202f1984 as part of the Oko programme, equipped with optical telescopes and infrared sensors to detect missile launches.', 'paragraph_anchor_or_comment': 'first paragraph after infobox'}, 'debiased': {'neutral_description_50_words_max': 'Kosmos\\u202f1581, launched on 3\\u202fJuly\\u202f1984 from Plesetsk, was a Soviet US‑K‑type early‑warning satellite in a Molniya orbit. Designed for four years, it was deactivated on 19\\u202fAugust\\u202f1985. It is cataloged as 1984‑071A (SATCAT\\u202f15095) and part of the Oko programme.', 'bias_comment': \"English article em