tion of responsibility and significance.\", 'languages_used': ['en'], 'perspectives': [{'language': 'en', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finnair_Flight_915', 'key_points': ['**Pilot testimony fuels a Cold‑War‑era allegation:** In 2014 two Finnair pilots publicly claimed that a Soviet missile locked onto their DC‑10 over Svalbard on 23\\u202fDecember\\u202f1987, detonating a mere seconds before a near‑miss. Their account, released decades after the flight, frames the event as a deliberate, possibly experimental, Soviet attack on a civilian aircraft.', '**Official silence and “Finlandization” controversy:** Finnish ministers, the security services and aviation authorities were reportedly unaware of the incident until the 2014 press coverage. Critics argue that the Cold‑War practice of “Finlandization” kept the matter hidden, labeling the lack of reporting a grave breach of duty and a cover‑up.', '**Technical debate remains inconclusive:** Experts dispute the missile’s type and launch platform—ranging from a surface‑to‑air system fired from a vessel or submarine to a wayward test rocket—while noting that the described explosion and flight‑path changes do not match known Soviet weapons of the era.', '**No casualties, but lasting political fallout:** Although the flight landed safely with all 219 occupants unharmed, the delayed revelation sparked outrage, condemnation from former ministers, and renewed scrutiny of how aviation threats are reported in Finland today.', '**Historical context of Arctic over‑flight:** The incident occurred on a pioneering non‑stop Tokyo‑Helsinki route that avoided Soviet‑controlled airspace, underscoring the geopolitical tension surrounding Arctic air routes during the late‑Cold‑War period.']}]}}, {'seed': {'name': 'SDI', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SDI'}, 'extracted': {'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SDI', 'name': 'Strategic Defense Initiative', 'years': '1983-1993', 'short_description': 'U.S. anti‑missile program announced by President Reagan in 1983 to develop space‑based and ground‑based systems for defending against ballistic missiles, popularly dubbed “Star\\xa0Wars.”', 'paragraph_anchor_or_comment': \"bullet under 'In science and technology' list\"}, 'debiased': {'neutral_description_50_words_max': 'The Strategic Defense Initiative, announced by U.S. President Ronald\\u202fReagan in 1983, aimed to develop a space‑based missile‑defense system. It operated until 1993, encountering technical hurdles, high costs, and criticism for potentially intensifying the Cold‑War arms race.', 'bias_comment': 'English and French entries foreground the Cold‑War and \"Star Wars\" narrative, while Russian adds historical context of U.S.–Soviet competition. Hebrew and Chinese pages emphasize unrelated technical meanings of the SDI acronym, reflecting local editorial priorities and possibly downplaying the initiative’s geopolitical controversy. These language‑specific emphases illustrate how cultural and disciplinary lenses shape the presentation of the same term.', 'languages_used': ['en', 'fr', 'he', 'ru', 'zh'], 'perspectives': [{'language': 'en', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SDI', 'key_points': ['**A catch‑all acronym:** “SDI” is used for a wildly diverse set of things—video games, companies, scientific terms, and even an airport code—showing how widely the abbreviation spreads across fields.', '**Corporate and organizational usage dominates:** Major firms and groups such as Samsung\\u202fSDI (batteries), Steel Dynamics, Scuba Diving International, and the political party Socialisti Democratici Italiani all rely on the SDI shorthand.', '**Technology\\u202f/\\u202fcomputing is a key sector:** In tech circles SDI can mean anything from a Serial Digital Interface for video, a Single Document Interface UI style, to Software‑Defined Infrastructure and Spatial Data Infrastructure.', '**Scientific and niche applications abound:** The letters also label specialized concepts like Selective Dissemination of Information, Silt Density Index (RO systems), Subsurface Drip Irrigation, and even the historic Strategic Defense Initiative.']}, {'language': 'fr', 'url': 'https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/SDI', 'key_points': ['**SDI\\u202f: un sigle polyvalent** – la combinaison de trois lettres désigne des notions très diverses, tant en français qu’en anglais, dans des domaines techniques, institutionnels ou commerciaux.', '**Informatique & connectique** – les usages les plus courants sont *Serial Digital Interface* (protocole vidéo numérique) et *Single Document Interface* (architecture d’interface utilisateur).', '**Organisations et infrastructures** – il désigne notamment le *Sarawak Development Institute* et la *Spatial Data Infrastructure*, une architecture de données géographiques partagées.', '**En français** – le sigle recouvre le *Schéma Directeur Informatique*, le *Système de Détection Incendie*, ainsi que des syndicats professionnels (distributeurs indépendants, indépendants & TPE).', '**En anglais** – parmi les sens les plus emblématiques figurent *Scuba Diving International*, la fameuse *Strategic Defense Initiative* («\\u202fguerre des étoiles\\u202f») et le *SDI* (moteur atmosphérique à injection diesel).']}, {'language': 'he', 'url': 'https://he.wikipedia.org/wiki/SDI', 'key_points': ['**תשתית מוגדרת תוכנה (SDI)** – מודל של תשתית מחשוב שמנוהלת באופן מלא בעזרת קוד, ללא צורך בהתערבות ידנית או תלות במוגבלויות חומרתיות ספציפיות.', '**הגדרה הצהרית של דרישות** – הצרכים של היישום (פונקציונליים ולא‑פונקציונליים) מתוארים במפורש, מה שמאפשר למערכת לבצע בפריסה אוטומטית את המשאבים והחומרה הדרושים כדי לעמוד בהם.', '**תנאי קדם** – פריסות SDI דורשות בדרך כלל מחשוב ענן ורשת מוגדרת תוכנה (SDN) כאסטרטגיה בסיסית להפעלה.', '**יתרונות מרכזיים** – צמצום משמעותי של עלויות ו‑מאמץ בתחזוקת תשתיות IT, רשת וחומרה; הגדלת עקביות, יכולת הרחבה, פריסה מרחוק ללא זמן השבתה, וניצול כלי גרסאות (כגון\\u202fGit).', '**יכולת שינוי ללא השבתה** – באמצעות חישוב אוטומטי של שינויי המצב בין תצורות