al protection while omitting local perspectives on the Royal Navy’s presence. Other language versions (e.g., French, German) may highlight technical specifications or broader strategic contexts, showing national historiographical biases.', 'languages_used': ['en'], 'perspectives': [{'language': 'en', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HMS_Goldfinch_(1889)', 'key_points': ['**A modest‑size, late‑Victorian gunboat:** HMS\\u202fGoldfinch was a Redbreast‑class gunboat built at Sheerness (launched 18\\u202fMay\\u202f1889, cost £39,300) with a 13‑knot speed and a mixed sail/steam propulsion system.', '**Imperial policing on the Australia Station:** From March\\u202f1890 to August\\u202f1899 she served on the Australia Station, exemplifying the Royal Navy’s use of small gunboats to patrol and protect far‑flung colonies.', '**Shift to scientific duties:** Converted to a survey vessel in January\\u202f1902, she was recommissioned under Commander Frederick\\u202fCharles\\u202fLearmonth and carried out hydrographic work in the Mediterranean, the West African coast, and other overseas waters—showing how aging combat ships were repurposed for peacetime tasks.', '**Rapid obsolescence and disposal:** By 1906 the vessel was deemed unfit for further service; the newer sloop HMS\\u202fMutine replaced her as a survey ship, and Goldfinch was sold for breaking on 14\\u202fMay\\u202f1907, underscoring the short operational life of Victorian‑era gunboats as naval technology advanced.']}]}}, {'seed': {'name': 'Talk:Ching Cheong - Wikipedia', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ching_Cheong'}, 'extracted': {'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Ching_Cheong', 'name': 'Talk:Ching Cheong - NPOV dispute (July 2005)', 'years': '2005', 'short_description': 'In July 2005 editors debated the neutral‑point‑of‑view on the Ching Cheong article, questioning his birthplace, nationality and the description of his detention, leading to edits, source disputes and removal of the NPOV tag.', 