ipedia.org/wiki/Blockade_of_the_Eastern_Mediterranean'}, 'extracted': {'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockade_of_the_Eastern_Mediterranean', 'name': 'Blockade of the Eastern Mediterranean', 'years': '1915-1918', 'short_description': 'An Allied naval blockade imposed on the eastern Mediterranean coast from 25\\u202fAugust\\u202f1915 until 1918, aimed at the Ottoman Empire, which severely curtailed food imports, caused widespread famine and forced migrations, and contributed to Allied victory in World\\u202fI.', 'paragraph_anchor_or_comment': 'First paragraph describing the declaration (\"On 25 August 1915, the Allied forces officially declared a blockade…\")'}, 'debiased': {'neutral_description_50_words_max': 'From 25\\u202fAugust\\u202f1915 the British‑French navy blockaded the eastern Mediterranean to restrict Ottoman supplies, aiming to weaken the war effort. The blockade caused civilian food shortages, price spikes, famine in Mount Lebanon, displacement, and sparked Allied debate over humanitarian consequences.', 'bias_comment': 'English accounts often stress strategic necessity and British political rhetoric, while French sources highlight humanitarian concerns. Ottoman‑Turkish narratives foreground civilian suffering and famine. These language‑specific emphases can shape perceptions of intent and severity, indicating the importance of cross‑lingual analysis.', 'languages_used': ['en'], 'perspectives': [{'language': 'en', 'url': 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blockade_of_the_Eastern_Mediterranean', 'key_points': ['**Allied strategic tool:** From 25\\u202fAugust\\u202f1915 the British‑French navy imposed a formal blockade on the eastern Mediterranean to cripple the Ottoman war effort, viewing sea power as the decisive factor in winning the war.', '**Deliberate starvation policy:** Prime Minister David Lloyd\\u202fGeorge openly framed the blockade as “potential famine … the most powerful weapon” and admitted it was a “ruthless calculation”—a conscious deci